# Keep CSVs byte-exact across platforms.
#
# core.autocrlf=true rewrote eval/splits/*.csv with CRLF on checkout. Their
# `scoring_points` column is a multi-line quoted field, so every expected answer
# gained a trailing \r -- and score.py extracts scoring points with `([^\n]+)`,
# which captures the \r as part of the string. "node-6" then never equals
# "node-6\r" and EVERY case scored 0.000, silently, on a correct answer.
# Judged runs are unaffected (judges supply their own query.csv), but our own
# eval and anything reproducing REPORT.md's tables are not.
*.csv -text
